            <ArticleTitle>Hepatic primary neuroendocrine carcinoma: about a new case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>254</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11604/pamj.2015.20.254.5710</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a new case of Primary hepatic neuroendocrine carcinoma admitted in our hospital and revealed in 53 years man by epigastric pain and flush syndrome. A liver biopsy with immunohistochemical study confirmed the original location of a neuroendocrine carcinoma. After 12 cures of Chemotherapy and a follow up of 12 months, the patient is still in complete remission.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
